{"type":"text","timestamp":1790447954654,"sessionID":"ses_f21008f31ffeSIHOrjs2VT1Blx","part":{"id":"prt_0df03aacc001oSGFcAUx489W10","messageID":"msg_0df037838001zuibhyUYF3aTGG","sessionID":"ses_f21008f31ffeSIHOrjs2VT1Blx","type":"text","text":"Task complete. I updated `/workspace/scripts/entities/tank/weapon/bullet.gd` to match the specification exactly:\n\n```gdscript\nextends Area2D\nclass_name Bullet\n\nconst SPEED = 500\n\nvar direction: Vector2 = Vector2.ZERO\nvar tank: Tank\n\nfunc _physics_process(delta):\n\tposition += direction.normalized() * SPEED * delta\n\nfunc _on_area_entered(_area):\n\tqueue_free()\n\nfunc _on_body_entered(body):\n\tif body is Crate:\n\t\tbody.destroy()\n\tqueue_free()\n```\n\nIt fulfills every requirement:\n- `const SPEED = 500`\n- Stores travel `direction` and the firing `tank`\n- Moves every physics frame via `direction.normalized() * SPEED * delta`\n- `area_entered` → `queue_free()`\n- `body_entered` → destroys `Crate` bodies via `body.destroy()` before `queue_free()`\n\nVerification performed:\n- Headless `--check-only` parse passed with exit code 0 and no script errors\n- Running the project showed no errors\n- Frame captures confirmed the bullet spawns at the tank, travels rightward with the physics movement code, and the bullet/despawn behavior works (bullets disappear before/after reaching obstacles as signals fire), with the scene rendering correctly throughout.","time":{"start":1790447954636,"end":1790447954638},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"resp_e696be148ff044f8b78e286190fd8284_msg"}}}}
